By trial: the smallest positive integer whose square ends in 269,696 is 25,264,
whose square is 638,269,696.

Digit by digit: every number whose square ends in 269,696 ends in one of
025264 099736 150264 224736 275264 349736 400264 474736 525264 599736 650264 724736 775264 849736 900264 974736
so the smallest such positive number is 25,264.

Babbage's guess, 99,736, squared is 9,947,269,696: it does end in 269,696,
but 25,264 is smaller, so Babbage's answer was not the smallest.
